.TH st80 1 "24 July 1989"
.SH NAME
Objectworks for Smalltalk-80
.SH SYNOPSIS	
.B st80
[
.I options 
] 
.B st80.im 
.br
.B st80
[
.I options 
] 
.I localImageName 
.SH DESCRIPTION 
.BI st80 
takes the virtual image file name as its argument; this may be 
the standard Smalltalk-80 system virtual image (usually 
.BI /usr/smalltalk/image/st80.im 
or simply, 
.BI st80.im
), or a customized snapshot version of the virtual image.  It may 
also take options (see below). 
.SH OPTIONS 
.TP
\fB-a \fInumber\fR
	Address space warning.  If set, a low space notifier appears when the address 
space grows by \fInumber\fR bytes.  Useful to keep tabs on space consumption.
.TP
\fB-g \fInumber	\fR
	The maximum amount of time allowed for automatic garbage collection 
(expressed as a percentage of the total time of the computation).  For example, with -g 10, if the last garbage collection took 2 seconds, another 
garbage collection would not start until at least 20 seconds had elapsed and space 
was getting low.  Or, -g 0 suppresses the automatic mark-and-sweep garbage collector entirely.  The -g switch does not affact the primary storage reclamation system, a generation scavenger, which should be invisible to the system user.
.TP
\fB-h \fInumber	\fR
	Height.  Sets the height of the Smalltalk window when the system comes up 
(in pixels).  By default, the Smalltalk window will be the full size of 
the display.
.TP
\fB-l \fInumber	\fR
	Size of the large-object zone.  If set, the size of the zone in which
large-objects are 
housed will be \fInumber\fR bytes.  The default large-object zone size varies from platform to platform (typically hundreds of KB).
.TP
\fB-m \fInumber	\fR
	Total space allocated to object memory (in bytes).  If you use this switch,
you will 
be given exactly this amount of space at startup time and no more thereafter.  
The -m switch disables the default mechanism that starts the system with an 
object memory large enough to hold the image and then increases object memory 
as necessary.  The -m switch is useful both for limiting address space
consumption and guaranteeing access to an adequate amount of address space.
.TP
\fB-n \fInumber	\fR
	Native-method zone size.  If set, the native-method zone size will be \fInumber\fR bytes.  The default native-method 
zone size varies from platform to platform, ranging from approximately 400 KB to more than double that.
.TP
\fB-s \fInumber	\fR
	Number of stacks.  If set, there will be \fInumber\fR stacks.  By default there are 30.
.TP
\fB-v \fR
	Version information.  Reports detailed version/release codes meaningful
to ParcPlace customer-support personnel.
.TP
\fB-w \fInumber	\fR
	Sets the width of the Smalltalk window when the system comes up 
(in pixels).  By default, the Smalltalk window will be the full size of 
the display.
